# `Cargo.lock` is TRACKED (#613) — it was ignored here from the scaffold commit (#259) with no
# rationale, which left the one crate that ships a compiled binary to a registry as the only one
# whose dependency graph was resolved fresh at every publish. Nothing consumes this crate as a Rust
# library (`publish = false`; see docs/agents/release.md), so the "libraries do not commit a lock"
# convention does not apply — what npm receives is the build output, and the lock is the only record
# of what went into it.
